spec hz03-aborted-versions-withdrawn: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# HZ03. s1 sets x.v = 1 and rolls back; the vacuum is drained (H1). s2 reads x and
# then writes x.v = 2 in autocommit statements. No reader ever sees v = 1; s2's write
# is refused only while s1's version is in flight, and succeeds once it is withdrawn.

starting permutation: s1w s1rb s1dr s2r s2w
step s1w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'x'}) SET n.v = 1 RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s1dr: <vacuum drain>
step s2r: MATCH (n:Item {name:'x'}) RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
